From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:40:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] feat(ui): put away the team and product chrome on a
 one-person instance

This doop is used for the canvas (sign-up is closed; one person and their
agents), so the entry points to what was built for teams and the hosted
product are hidden: "Owned by me" / "Shared with me", Community,
Automations and Integrations (rail), owner/member avatar stacks on canvas
tiles, the plan line in the account menu, Share (canvas top bar, phone
menu, canvas tile menu), the canvas Help menu (docs, support chat) and the
Webhooks settings pane (rail entry and the phone's tab), the Desktop app
and Website links in the account menu. On the home page, the rail's Agents section (agent
list and "Connect an agent") and the "Ask me what to design" hero (chips
and prompt composer) are gone too; the canvas list, Import and New canvas
stay.

Kept on purpose: workspaces (rail section, "Move to workspace"), the
presence pill (it is also where a working agent shows), comments, the Doop
Agent, Activity, Memory, Connect AI on the canvas and Agent keys (the host's
MCP key is one).

Only the ways in are hidden: the pages still open by URL and the server
is unchanged, so none of this is a permission. One flag, FULL_UI in
src/lib/fullUi.ts, guards every spot; localStorage['doop:full-ui'] = 'on'
and a reload bring the full UI back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
